ALWAYS reference the TASKS.md file at the root of the project before working on any code.

This file contains:
- Current task statuses (PENDING, IN_PROGRESS, COMPLETED)
- Detailed task descriptions and acceptance criteria
- System architecture information
- Integration points between components
- Code reference examples

When working on tasks:
1. Only work on tasks with status PENDING and priority HIGH when all dependencies are COMPLETED
2. Update task status from PENDING to IN_PROGRESS when starting work
3. Update task status from IN_PROGRESS to COMPLETED when finished
4. Add implementation notes in the NOTES section of each completed task
5. Reference existing code patterns from the CODE REFERENCE section

The algorithmic trading system has three main components:
- Model 1: Stock Screener (Already implemented)
- Model 2: Portfolio Optimizer (Partially implemented)
- Model 3: Meta-Optimizer (Not yet implemented)
- EC2 PyMC Server (Not yet implemented)